    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbafcStaffalsoa]{Staff}, Legendary (Requires Attunement by a Cleric)</em></p><p>This staff has two forms: a shadowy state known as <em>Anathema</em> and a holy state known as <em>Benediction</em>. While attuned to the staff, you can switch the staff from one state to the other at dawn.</p><p><strong>Anathema.</strong> As <em>Anathema</em>, the staff grants the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Necrotic Resistance.</strong> While attuned to the staff, you have Resistance to Necrotic damage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Shadow Mana.</strong> While you’re holding the staff, when you cast a level 1–5 spell from the Necromancy school that would expend a spell slot, you can roll 1d6. If the number on the die exceeds the spell’s level, the spell slot isn’t expended.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Benediction.</strong> As <em>Benediction</em>, the staff grants the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Radiant Resistance.</strong> While attuned to the staff, you have Resistance to Radiant Damage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Light-Blessed Healing.</strong> While you’re holding the staff, when you cast a spell that would restore Hit Points to a creature, you can treat the spell as if it had been cast using a spell slot of 1 level higher.</p></li></ul><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-Sqod7paVFgH9ZLqw\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Le bâton commence en <em>Anathema</em>. Pour changer d’état à l’aube, activez l’autre effet et désactivez celui-ci dans l’onglet <em>Effects</em> de l’objet. <em>Shadow Mana</em> lance le d6 : si le résultat dépasse le niveau du sort, rendez l’emplacement à la main. Pour <em>Light-Blessed Healing</em>, ajoutez à la main les soins d’un emplacement d’un niveau de plus.</p></section>",
